<title>DUBAI: UAE expects 1998 oil price of $18-20 barrel.</title>
<headline>UAE expects 1998 oil price of $18-20 barrel.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Arab Emirates Petroleum and Mineral Resources Minister Obaid bin Saif al-Nasseri on Wednesday forecast average oil prices of between $18-20 a barrel in 1998, the official UAE news agency WAM said.</p>
<p>International benchmark North Sea dated Brent crude was trading at $18.40 on Wednesday and has averaged around $20 a barrel so far this year.</p>
<p>Al-Nasseri, speaking after a board meeting of a local state petroleum firm, added that oil prices had been helped by an awareness in OPEC of the need for commitment to quotas.</p>
<p>OPEC-member UAE derives about 75 percent of its revenue from oil and main emirate Abu Dhabi is one of a few producers that has spare production capacity.</p>
</text>
